  "sale_events": [],
  "body": "Built in 2019 and positioned within one of Castor Bay’s most desirable and tightly held family locations just moments from Kennedy Park, this beautifully maintained home, designed by Creative Arch architects, presents an exceptional opportunity for families seeking quality, privacy and effortless modern living.\r\n\r\nThe home steps gently down its site, connecting beautifully with the surrounding native landscape while capturing excellent natural light. Vertical timber cladding complements the bush setting, while extensive glazing frames the ferns and ponga, creating a home that feels warm, private and perfectly at ease within its environment.\r\n\r\nInside, expansive double-glazed joinery and a striking double-height entrance void draw light deep into the home. Framed views across the adjoining native reserve provide a peaceful backdrop throughout.\r\n\r\nAccommodation is superbly configured with four generous bedrooms, three bathrooms and three separate living areas. A lower-level bedroom and full bathroom offer excellent flexibility for guests, teenagers, extended family or those considering future single-level living, while the spacious master suite enjoys its own ensuite. \r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home, the open-plan kitchen, dining and family living area features premium Neff appliances, a generous scullery and excellent storage. Living flows effortlessly to a substantial entertainer’s deck, providing superb indoor-outdoor connection and a tranquil bush outlook. \r\n\r\nEngineered oak flooring, quality finishes, landscaped grounds, double garaging and excellent storage complete the package.\r\n\r\nZoned for both Westlake Boys and Westlake Girls High Schools, this is a rare opportunity to secure a near-new home combining architectural integrity, family functionality and exceptional privacy in one of the North Shore’s most sought-after coastal locations.\r\n\r\nIF YOU CAN'T REACH ANDREW DORREEN, PLEASE CONTACT HIS SALES ASSOCIATE ANNA JONES ON 021 489 171",
